# Which benchmarks are meant to exist, as `package<TAB>name<TAB>file`.
#
# One row per DECLARATION, not per benchmark identity. A package may define one
# benchmark name in mutually exclusive platform files — a `_linux_test.go` and
# a `_windows_test.go` — and collapsing those to a single row would make
# deleting either of them invisible here, since the surviving one keeps the
# identity alive. The deletion this file exists to expose is exactly that.
#
# scripts/run_benchmarks.sh compares this file against everything it can find
# in the tree and fails until the two agree. The comparison is what makes a
# DELETED benchmark loud: an enumeration checked only against itself would
# simply produce a smaller set, match everything in it, and report success.
#
# It is also what makes a benchmark this platform cannot compile visible at
# all. A `//go:build windows` benchmark cannot be enumerated by anything
# running on a Linux runner, so every tracked test file is instead PARSED —
# go/parser has no build configuration to be blind to — and go/build says which
# of those files this configuration would actually compile. Anything that
# exists but cannot be built here is listed below too, alongside an entry in
# BENCHMARKS_NOT_RUN_IN_CI saying it cannot run.
#
# Adding, removing or MOVING a benchmark fails CI until this file is updated in
# the same change. That is the point — the diff here is the only place anyone
# states that a benchmark is meant to be gone rather than accidentally
# missing.
#
# To update: run scripts/run_benchmarks.sh and apply the diff it prints. There
# is no regeneration command, deliberately: one would have to run under every
# build configuration to be correct, and a command that is right on Linux and
# quietly wrong on Windows is worse than a diff a human applies.
github.com/shardpilot/shardpilot-go	BenchmarkBuildBatchMapPayloads	client_benchmark_test.go
github.com/shardpilot/shardpilot-go	BenchmarkCompressBatchBody	request_compression_test.go
github.com/shardpilot/shardpilot-go	BenchmarkEnqueueMapPayload	client_benchmark_test.go
github.com/shardpilot/shardpilot-go	BenchmarkStatsCollectorAggregation	client_benchmark_test.go
github.com/shardpilot/shardpilot-go/pkg/crash	BenchmarkClientEmit	pkg/crash/client_test.go
